scripts/paint/paint.mjs generates src/styles/paint.css, the brush-paint textures of the general version (data pages
only): six static SVG stroke tiles (red, blue and yellow, horizontal and vertical) and the frayed outline used with
-webkit-mask-box-image. It is a line-for-line port of the owner-approved v5 prototype's paint-tex.py (notes:
owner-assets/data-redesign/v5/), including Python's seeded random for the outline, so the output equals the
prototype's. Run `node scripts/paint/paint.mjs --write` after changing a pigment (its base must match --ed-red,
--ed-blue or --ed-yellow in tokens.css), `--check` to compare the committed file, `--lab <file>` for a swatch sheet;
tests/unit/paint.test.ts checks the file, the pigments and the contrast bound of text on the paint.
